WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.133 --> 00:00:01.267
Russia is stepping

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:03.303
up recruitment for its war on Ukraine

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:05.405
with a new social media video

00:00:15.982 --> 00:00:18.118
it appears to mock men

00:00:18.118 --> 00:00:20.653
into leaving their everyday jobs

00:00:20.653 --> 00:00:22.789
like security guards and taxi drivers

00:00:22.789 --> 00:00:26.760
to become, quote, real men in combat.

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:30.196
CNN's Clare Sebastian is live in London.

00:00:31.431 --> 00:00:33.566
Clare, great to see you.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:35.769
I don't have much reaction there

00:00:35.769 --> 00:00:37.804
except for it seems,

00:00:37.804 --> 00:00:39.539
you know, whatever they think will work.

00:00:39.539 --> 00:00:40.473
But what's the response

00:00:40.473 --> 00:00:42.776
been online and in real life?

00:00:44.144 --> 00:00:46.012
Well, this is a pretty new campaign.

00:00:46.012 --> 00:00:48.014
That video came out just two days ago.

00:00:48.014 --> 00:00:49.582
So it's hard to assess at the moment

00:00:49.582 --> 00:00:51.451
its impact as a recruitment tool.

00:00:51.451 --> 00:00:53.219
But it's very clear

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:54.754
that this is designed to recruit men

00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:57.223
directly into the war in Ukraine.

00:00:57.223 --> 00:00:59.359
The Ministry of Defense uses the tagline,

00:00:59.359 --> 00:00:59.959
which in Russian

00:00:59.959 --> 00:01:00.727
translates roughly

00:01:00.727 --> 00:01:01.561
as join

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:03.897
your own and plays on the Russian acronym

00:01:04.164 --> 00:01:05.665
for special military operations.

00:01:05.665 --> 00:01:07.033
So there's no doubt that look,

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:07.700
I think

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:09.302
to be fair, a lot of armies

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:09.903
do use

00:01:09.903 --> 00:01:10.670
recruitment videos

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:11.805
that play on the ideas

00:01:11.805 --> 00:01:14.340
of confidence, of strength, of manhood

00:01:14.841 --> 00:01:15.608
in some ways.

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:17.143
But this also speaks

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:18.778
to Russia's challenges

00:01:18.778 --> 00:01:20.547
that it's having in recruiting

00:01:20.547 --> 00:01:22.449
trained personnel for the battlefield.

00:01:22.449 --> 00:01:22.982
We saw

00:01:22.982 --> 00:01:24.317
with that recruitment drive

00:01:24.317 --> 00:01:25.151
back in the autumn

00:01:25.151 --> 00:01:26.820
that they recruited 300,000

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:28.221
untrained personnel.

00:01:28.221 --> 00:01:29.089
I think this is an

00:01:29.089 --> 00:01:31.157
entirely different kind of recruitment

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:31.858
that we're seeing now

00:01:31.858 --> 00:01:33.760
using the special military operation,

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:35.028
the war in Ukraine,

00:01:35.028 --> 00:01:37.197
as a recruitment drive in itself.

00:01:37.197 --> 00:01:38.264
We know they're trying to swell

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:40.233
the ranks of their professional army

00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:42.135
by about 400,000 men.

00:01:42.135 --> 00:01:42.635
So clearly

00:01:42.635 --> 00:01:43.937
they are committing

00:01:43.937 --> 00:01:47.307
also these kind of PR resources to that.

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:48.942
Obviously, it's jarring

00:01:48.942 --> 00:01:50.477
looking at it from outside of Russia,

00:01:50.477 --> 00:01:51.544
knowing what we know

00:01:51.544 --> 00:01:52.846
about the kinds of casualties

00:01:52.846 --> 00:01:54.647
they're facing on the battlefield.

00:01:54.647 --> 00:01:55.782
The latest Pentagon

00:01:55.782 --> 00:01:57.817
documents, documents suggesting

00:01:57.817 --> 00:01:59.719
that about 43,000

00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:02.455
Russians have been killed in combat.

00:02:02.489 --> 00:02:03.690
That's just an estimate.

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:04.090
But I think

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:05.725
inside Russia, it's

00:02:05.725 --> 00:02:06.526
worth noting that

00:02:06.526 --> 00:02:08.128
a public service

00:02:08.128 --> 00:02:10.063
announcements are pretty common

00:02:10.063 --> 00:02:10.763
and secondly,

00:02:10.763 --> 00:02:11.998
that it is a country

00:02:11.998 --> 00:02:13.900
with very defined gender roles.

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:14.601
So I think

00:02:14.601 --> 00:02:16.202
that play on the idea of manliness

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:17.504
may be more effective

00:02:17.504 --> 00:02:18.938
than it seems from the outside.

00:02:18.938 --> 00:02:19.072
Well,

00:02:19.072 --> 00:02:19.672
and you touched on

00:02:19.672 --> 00:02:21.541
the very serious aspect of this,

00:02:21.541 --> 00:02:24.010
which is there is a marked difference

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:25.111
from what is being displayed

00:02:25.111 --> 00:02:25.778
in AD versus

00:02:25.778 --> 00:02:27.447
the reality on the ground

00:02:27.447 --> 00:02:28.581
of the battlefield.

00:02:28.581 --> 00:02:30.116
Clare Sebastian, thank you so much.

00:02:31.551 --> 00:02:33.453
Ukraine is making a new push to do

00:02:33.453 --> 00:02:34.787
one of the things that Russia tries

00:02:34.787 --> 00:02:35.355
to prevent

00:02:35.355 --> 00:02:38.158
with this invasion to join NATO allies.

00:02:38.158 --> 00:02:39.225
The secretary general paid

00:02:39.225 --> 00:02:39.492
a visit

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:40.593
to Kiev on Thursday

00:02:40.593 --> 00:02:42.962
and met with President Vladimir Zelensky,

00:02:42.962 --> 00:02:44.831
who made a new pitch for joining NATO's,

00:02:44.831 --> 00:02:47.066
which could put it on a path

00:02:47.066 --> 00:02:49.335
to a military conflict with Moscow.

00:02:49.335 --> 00:02:50.837
The NATO's leader didn't offer

00:02:50.837 --> 00:02:53.239
any timelines to key, but did say this

00:02:55.341 --> 00:02:56.943
Ukraine's future

00:02:56.943 --> 00:02:58.811
is in the Euro-Atlantic family.

00:02:58.811 --> 00:03:00.947
Ukraine's future is in NATO's.

00:03:02.882 --> 00:03:04.717
Moscow responded to Stoltenberg visit

00:03:04.717 --> 00:03:05.185
saying that

00:03:05.185 --> 00:03:05.852
keeping Ukraine

00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:06.853
out of NATO's remains

00:03:06.853 --> 00:03:08.688
one of its military goals.

00:03:08.688 --> 00:03:09.322
Now, Ukraine's

00:03:09.322 --> 00:03:11.291
allies are meeting in Germany to consider

00:03:11.291 --> 00:03:12.225
next steps

00:03:12.225 --> 00:03:13.159
in their assistance

00:03:13.159 --> 00:03:14.427
to give US Defense

00:03:14.427 --> 00:03:15.595
Secretary Lloyd Austin

00:03:15.595 --> 00:03:16.930
just spoke ahead of the meeting

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:18.898
of the Ukraine Defense Contact Group.

00:03:18.898 --> 00:03:20.934
It's happening at the Ramstein Air Base

00:03:20.934 --> 00:03:21.834
with defense ministers

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:22.835
and other officials

00:03:22.835 --> 00:03:25.638
from more than 50 countries taking part.

00:03:26.272 --> 00:03:27.407
And this all comes as we're

00:03:27.407 --> 00:03:27.907
getting word

00:03:27.907 --> 00:03:29.108
of a new Russian drone

00:03:29.108 --> 00:03:31.311
strike on Ukraine's capital.

00:03:31.311 --> 00:03:33.079
Sebastian is covering this for us

00:03:33.079 --> 00:03:34.113
this morning.

00:03:34.113 --> 00:03:35.348
Clare, what is the Lansky

00:03:35.348 --> 00:03:36.683
hoping will be achieved

00:03:36.683 --> 00:03:38.651
at this meeting about Ukraine?

00:03:38.651 --> 00:03:40.320
So the Rammstein Contact Group meeting,

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:42.222
this is all about coordinating

00:03:42.222 --> 00:03:44.424
and organizing new weapons supplies

00:03:44.424 --> 00:03:45.291
essentially for Ukraine.

00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:47.794
And I think his top priority right now

00:03:47.794 --> 00:03:49.162
is air defense.

00:03:49.162 --> 00:03:50.063
We know certainly

00:03:50.063 --> 00:03:51.965
and this is sort of uncomfortable context

00:03:51.965 --> 00:03:53.233
to the meeting for the US,

00:03:53.233 --> 00:03:53.633
but we know

00:03:53.633 --> 00:03:55.868
from those leaked Pentagon documents

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:58.004
that the belief is that

00:03:58.004 --> 00:03:59.339
while Ukraine might have

00:04:00.306 --> 00:04:01.241
a slight edge when it comes

00:04:01.241 --> 00:04:02.342
to ground forces

00:04:02.342 --> 00:04:03.309
because of the new weapons

00:04:03.309 --> 00:04:04.377
that it's been getting

00:04:04.377 --> 00:04:05.311
from the NATO allies,

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:06.980
the vulnerability is with air defense.

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:07.680
We've seen that

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:10.116
just now overnight with those attacks,

00:04:10.116 --> 00:04:11.851
the drone attacks on the capital

00:04:11.851 --> 00:04:12.452
for the first time,

00:04:12.452 --> 00:04:13.119
according to the head

00:04:13.119 --> 00:04:15.255
of the military administration, in Kiev,

00:04:15.321 --> 00:04:16.990
the first time in 25 days.

00:04:16.990 --> 00:04:18.625
But it is the second such overnight

00:04:18.625 --> 00:04:19.926
barrage of drones this week

00:04:19.926 --> 00:04:21.127
that continues to be

00:04:21.127 --> 00:04:22.061
a part of the playbook.

00:04:22.061 --> 00:04:24.197
They are pushing for more air defense

00:04:24.631 --> 00:04:25.698
And I think the second thing

00:04:25.698 --> 00:04:27.000
coming off that NATO

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:27.934
meeting in Kiev

00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:28.701
with the NATO secretary

00:04:28.701 --> 00:04:29.402
general, who, by the way,

00:04:29.402 --> 00:04:30.603
has just arrived

00:04:30.603 --> 00:04:32.505
at Ramstein, is security guarantees

00:04:32.505 --> 00:04:34.140
ahead of that summit in Vilnius.

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:34.340
Take a

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:35.508
listen to what Jens Stoltenberg

00:04:35.508 --> 00:04:36.776
had to say just a few moments ago.

00:04:38.578 --> 00:04:39.412
Press the incidents.

00:04:39.412 --> 00:04:41.114
Can I also

00:04:41.114 --> 00:04:43.883
discuss the preparations for the upcoming

00:04:44.183 --> 00:04:46.919
NATO summit in Vilnius in July?

00:04:47.887 --> 00:04:50.456
I have invited him to attend the meeting,

00:04:50.456 --> 00:04:52.592
and I'm glad that he has accepted

00:04:52.592 --> 00:04:53.660
the invitation

00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:55.395
and will attend the

00:04:55.395 --> 00:04:57.297
NATO summit in Vilnius.

00:04:57.297 --> 00:04:58.998
All NATO's allies have agreed

00:04:58.998 --> 00:05:02.969
that Ukraine will become a NATO member

00:05:05.171 --> 00:05:05.672
Well, president

00:05:05.838 --> 00:05:06.739
he attending the NATO's

00:05:06.739 --> 00:05:09.075
summit in Vilnius in Lithuania in July.

00:05:09.108 --> 00:05:11.177
Will certainly be very unwelcome optics

00:05:11.177 --> 00:05:12.211
for Moscow.

00:05:12.211 --> 00:05:13.546
The NATO's secretary general

00:05:13.546 --> 00:05:14.981
also saying he expects more weapons

00:05:14.981 --> 00:05:16.015
pledges this week.

00:05:16.015 --> 00:05:17.350
But he said that some of the focus

00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:18.051
will be on what he called

00:05:18.051 --> 00:05:19.419
the more boring stuff. Right.

00:05:19.419 --> 00:05:20.386
So sustaining

00:05:20.386 --> 00:05:21.654
the existing weapons platforms,

00:05:21.654 --> 00:05:23.823
they already have fuel ammunition,

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:25.591
maintenance, pass

00:05:25.591 --> 00:05:26.292
all of that stuff

00:05:26.292 --> 00:05:27.460
to to keep the things

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:28.461
they've already got

00:05:28.461 --> 00:05:29.896
going on the battlefield.

00:05:29.896 --> 00:05:31.464
Class, Sebastiaan, thank you so much.

